    "name": "One Foggy Christmas Eve",
    "rules": "Normal Sudoku Rules Apply\n\nCells separated by a Knight's move (in chess) cannot contain the same digit.\n\nDigits along an arrow must sum to the number in the circled cell. All arrows sum to a single digit number. Arrows may end on the same cell, but otherwise do not overlap or cross over each other.\n\nCells connected with a V must sum to 5.\nNot all possible V's are necessarily given.\n\nThe grid is covered in fog. Placing a correct number in the grid reveals its' surrounding cells. You may place digits in cells covered by fog, but no guessing is required."
